    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0167" n="51" xml:id="pg51"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/594.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires at
                            Tokyo to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-10-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 22, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Foreign Office very anxious that Government of United States recognize Japan is
                    absolutely sincere and aboveboard in her Chinese policy, and in desiring only to
                    protect Japanese subjects.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
